<title>HONDURAS: Honduran inflation two pct in January.</title>
<headline>Honduran inflation two pct in January.</headline>
<dateline>TEGUCIGALPA, Honduras 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Honduran inflation in January was two percent, compared with 0.5 percent the year before and 1.1 percent in December, the central bank said on Friday.</p>
<p>It said the consumer price index was pushed up by increases in the cost of food, healthcare, transport and housing. Economists said it complicated the task of meeting the government's official inflation target of 12 percent in 1997.</p>
<p>In 1996, inflation reached 24.9 percent.</p>
<p>((--Gustavo Palencia, Tegucigalpa newsroom +504 392885))</p>
